# COLUMNS behavior
select COALESCE(COLUMNS(*)) from (select NULL, 2, 3) t(a, b, c)
When the COLUMNS expression is expanded, the resulting query becomes:
D select COALESCE(a) a, COALESCE(b) b, COALESCE(c) c from (select NULL, 2, 3) t(a, b, c)
The result of this query is:
┌───────┬───────┬───────┐
│   a   │   b   │   c   │
│ int32 │ int32 │ int32 │
├───────┼───────┼───────┤
│       │     2 │     3 │
└───────┴───────┴───────┘

# *COLUMNS behavior
select COALESCE(*COLUMNS(*)) from (select NULL, 2, 3) t(a, b, c)
When the *COLUMNS expression is expanded, the resulting query becomes:
D select COALESCE(a, b, c) from (select NULL, 2, 3) t(a, b, c)
The result of this query is:
┌─────────────────────────┐
│ COALESCE(t.a, t.b, t.c) │
│          int32          │
├─────────────────────────┤
│                       2 │
└─────────────────────────┘

